2 ADDR
3 CITY Odense
1 OCCU Købmand, rådmand og borgmester i Odense, 
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} http://www.nermo.org/slekt/d0022/g0000044.html#I38082
2 CONT
2 CONT ABT 1565 - 1631
2 CONT
2 CONT     * OCCUPATION: Skriver hos Ludvig Munk i Trh. Borgermester i Odense
2 CONT
2 CONT     * BIRTH: ABT 1565, Odsense, Fyn ? (usikre foreldre)
2 CONT
2 CONT     * DEATH: 1631, ('i stor velstand')
2 CONT
2 CONT     * EVENT: Hadde et forhold til Ellen Marsvin (ca.1588-ca.1599) 
2 CONT
2 CONT ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
2 CONT
2 CONT Købmand, raadmand (nævnt 1604-1622) og borgmester (nævnt 162 2-1631) i Odense. Hadde et forhold til Ellen Marsvin (ca.1588-ca.1599), Skriver hos Ludvig Munk i Trh. Borgermester i Odense. “i stor velstand”.
2 CONT
2 CONT Bogen, "Konsistorialraad Jacob Christian Schmidth´s samtlige efterkommere" ved S. Otto Brenner: "Af dansk adel".
2 CONT
2 CONT From Knud Gether about Otte Knudsen: The country judge Jacob Bircherod writes that his father and mother died when he was 4 and 5 years old, so his older brother ..probably Rickert sent him in the Latin school in Odense.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was sent as a young man to a merchant in Hamburg for his early training or as they called it ..in scientiis civilibus....then he went to Holland , where his brother Hans was lieutenant colonel and served in during the war with 
2 CONC him. After this he sailed to Norway and became scribe with nobleman Ludvig Munk in Trondhjem.
2 CONT
2 CONT Ludvig Munk was in charge of Norway , he married the 17 years old Ellen Marsvin, who's father was  Rigsraad Jørgen Marsvin......(Ellen Marsvin owned Thurø) , Otto followed the family from Norway to Denmark and Ellen was only agree
2 CONC able to the marriage if Ludvig Munk would build a castle where she threw down her glow (glove?)!
2 CONT
2 CONT She was not hiding her interest in the 3 years older Otto, so her husband had for 3 months Otto jailed in the cellar of Odense Town hall, however Ellen arranged  music for Otto every evening.
2 CONT
2 CONT The big accident happened when her husband found Otto in her bedchamber, however she got out of that predicament by claiming that Otto was there to ask for her maid's hand in marriage..........so Otto now had to marry. In 1599 he 
2 CONC married Birgitte who seem to have come from a good family. The crest, a black timber weapon in a silver shield seems to indicate she is of the Skjalm Bangs family.
2 CONT
2 CONT Kirstine Munk was born on July 9 1598 born at Nørlund estate, he the 61 years old husband accepted the daughter as his after nine  years without a child and covered her in her birth with his family shield with the 3 roses. There i
2 CONC s very little doubt she is daughter of Otto.
2 CONT
2 CONT He now after marrying started as merchant in Odense and became its wealthiest citizen, with a house also in Kerteminde like his Brother.  He exported in 1616-1627 through the custom house in Aabenraa 4414 steers. In the old Odense
2 CONC  documents one finds the exist passport for his ships travels in the Baltic sea, he also rented the vine cellar under the Town hall by paying 24 RD every Xmas eve.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1618 he bought from his older sister her estate in Overgade which had been built by Oluf Bager in 1580. His wife must have died in 1613 with whom he had 5 children, because in this year October 4 he declares at the town hall th
2 CONC at want to settle his estate with his children and married the 2 nd time October 10.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was Lord Mayor of Odense 1622-31 and was buried in Sct Knuds Church , his gravestone  located ahead of the other noble family Ahlefeldt carried the name Seeblad
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Købmand, raadmand (nævnt 1604-1622) og borgmester (nævnt 162 2-1631) i Odense. Hadde et forhold til Ellen Marsvin (ca.1588-ca.1599), Skriver hos Ludvig Munk i Trh. Borgermester i Odense. “i stor velstand”. Bogen, "Konsistorialraad
2 CONC  Jacob Christian Schmidth´s samtlige efterkommere" ved S. Otto Brenner: "Af dansk adel".
2 CONT
2 CONT From Knud Gether about Otte Knudsen: The country judge Jacob Bircherod writes that his father and mother died when he was 4 and 5 years old, so his older brother ..probably Rickert sent him in the Latin school in Odense.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was sent as a young man to a merchant in Hamburg for his early training or as they called it ..in scientiis civilibus....then he went to Holland , where his brother Hans was lieutenant colonel and served in during the war with 
2 CONC him. After this he sailed to Norway and became scribe with nobleman Ludvig Munk in Trondhjem.
2 CONT
2 CONT Ludvig Munk was in charge of Norway , he married the 17 years old Ellen Marsvin, who's father was  Rigsraad Jørgen Marsvin......(Ellen Marsvin owned Thurø) , Otto followed the family from Norway to Denmark and Ellen was only agree
2 CONC able to the marriage if Ludvig Munk would build a castle where she threw down her glow!
2 CONT
2 CONT She was not hiding her interest in the 3 years older Otto, so her husband had for 3 months Otto jailed in the cellar of Odense Town hall, however Ellen arranged  music for Otto every evening.
2 CONT
2 CONT The big accident happened when her husband found Otto in her bedchamber, however she got out of that predicament by claiming that Otto was there to ask for her maid's hand in marriage..........so Otto now had to marry. In 1599 he 
2 CONC married Birgitte who seem to have come from a good family. The crest, a black timber weapon in a silver shield seems to indicate she is of the Skjalm Bangs family.
2 CONT
2 CONT Kirstine Munk was born on July 9 1598 born at Nørlund estate, he the 61 years old husband accepted the daughter as his after nine  years without a child and covered her in her birth with his family shield with the 3 roses. There i
2 CONC s very little doubt she is daughter of Otto.
2 CONT
2 CONT He now after marrying started as merchant in Odense and became its wealthiest citizen, with a house also in Kerteminde like his Brother.  He exported in 1616-1627 through the custom house in Aabenraa 4414 steers. In the old Odense
2 CONC  documents one finds the exist passport for his ships travels in the Baltic sea, he also rented the vine cellar under the Town hall by paying 24 RD every Xmas eve.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1618 he bought from his older sister her estate in Overgade which had been built by Oluf Bager in 1580. His wife must have died in 1613 with whom he had 5 children, because in this year October 4 he declares at the town hall th
2 CONC at want to settle his estate with his children and married the 2 nd time October 10.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was Lord Mayor of Odense 1622-31 and was buried in Sct Knuds Church , his gravestone  located ahead of the other noble family Ahlefeldt carried the name Seeblad
2 CONT *  22: Skifte efter Otte Knudsen, borgmester, Odense, 1634
2 CONT
2 CONT Skifteprotokol 1626-35, pag. 241r.
2 CONT
2 CONT Efterlod hustruen Abigael Hasebardt og børnene Karen Ottesdatter g.m. Poul Schinkel borgmester i Kerteminde, Jacob Ottesen og Birgitte Ottesdatter, der var mindreårige, Antoni Ottesen, ligeledes mindreårig, Knud Ottesen, borger i 
2 CONC Odense og en afdød datter Magdalenes børn: Jacob og Birthe Hasebardt samt Jørgen Ottesen, ligeledes umyndig. Ifølge dansk biografisk leksikon var Otte Knudsen Seeblad af adelig slægt, gift første gang med Birgitte Lauridsdatter (d
2 CONC . 1613).
2 CONT
2 CONT Borgmesteren døde 13. sep. 1631.
2 CONT
2 CONT Otto Knudsen, mayor of Odense, from a noble family in Funen. Married to Abigail Hasebardt, left behind both adult and young children: Karen, Jacob, Birgitte, Antoni, Knud, Jørgen and a deceased daughter Magdalene whose children in
2 CONC herited her part.
2 CONT
2 CONT Salig borgmesteres liffkleder: 1 bomesis kasiach med en snorer paa for … 6 sldr 1 gammell wbrugelig boratis kledning, trøye och buxer … 6 mk 1 gammell vdprichett tobinns trøye for … 1 sldr 1 boratis trøye for … 4 dr 1 gammell wbru
2 CONC gelig offuerkichs kledning for … 1 rdr 1 gammell wdpickeeritt fillisels kledning for … 1 rdr 1 gammell boratis kledning … 3½ dr 1 wdpickereeritt silcke groffgrøns kledning for … 10 dr Maarfoeder till wnderfoere 1 kaßiach med, huor
2 CONC  wdj waar 18 maar, achtett for … 22½ sldr 1 gammell boratis kledning … 1 rdr 1 gammell sabels lue for … 10 sldr 1 fellfors lue for … 10 sldr 1 faff fløyels kledning, trøye och buxer for … 36 sldr 1 gammell soerdt klede kledning fo
2 CONC r … 3 sldr 1 par fløyels wannter, wnderfaarridt med maaer foer … 8 sldr 1 klede kledning med en snooer paa, for … 5 dr 1 klede kledning … 6 dr 1 wdpickerridt atlaskis kledning for … 24 sldr 1 soerdt klede kaßioch, med en snoer paa
2 CONC  … 4 dr 1 gammell klede trøye med en snoer … 4 dr 1 fir traaes trøye … 2 dr 1 gammell offuerkichs trøye … 1 dr 1 gammell stuckett borettis trøye … 2 dr 1 gammell offuer kichs trøye … 1 dr 1 offuerkichs trøye … 6 mk 1 graae tobins 
2 CONC trøye … 6 dr 1 gammell wbrugelig offuerkichs trøye … 3 mk 1 blommidt armesins trøye … 6 dr 1 brun armesins natt trøye … 10 dr 1 par wdprickett fillisels buxer … 2 dr 1 gammell offuerkichs trøye … 3 mk 1 par gammell blommidt kaffs 
2 CONC buxer for … 6 dr 1 staalgraae klede trøye … 4 dr 1 offuer kichs trøye … 10 mmk 1 gammell offuer kichs trøye … 3 mk 1 fioll brun fillisels trøye … 2 dr 1 soertt klede kappe med adtlaschis kraffue … 10 sldr 1 klede kappe med slet fl
2 CONC øyell for vnder for … 50 sldr 1 klede kappe med boratt forneder for … 20 sldr 1 klede kappe med tesenell for wnder for … 15 sldr 1 gammell brun regenn kappe … 6 dr 1 groffgrøns kappe … 10 dr 1 blaae reiße kioell … 8 dr 1 brunn per
2 CONC pedeuandtz natt trøye … 8 dr 1 blaae bayes wldennschiortte wnderforett med graauerck for … 6 dr 1 huid bayes liiff, med ingenn ermer … 6 mk 1 par staallgraae strigsstrømper for … 2 dr 1 paar phioell bruen strigs strømper for … 6 m
2 CONC k 1 par gammell strigs strømper … 5 mk 1 par brune silche strømper … 6 sldr 1 par nye soerte sex traae strigs strømper for … 3 dr 1 brurn adtlaschis brøst dug, wnderfoeridt med floes for … 8 dr 1 par leder hanndsche, stuckett med 
2 CONC soert silcke for … 6 mk
