2 CONT He belonged to the lower nobility. 1 June 1442 he was one of 36 delegates from “the ordinary people” to a national meeting confirming the election of Kristoffer of Bavaria as the new King of Norway,  Sweden and Denmark. His name 
2 CONC Solve means “solved” or “saved”. The tradition is that it was given  to him because he survived the great plague The Black Death of 1349/50; just after he was born.  Another version is that it was his mother who survived the plagu
2 CONC e, and that he was born prematurely just afterwards, but nevertheless grew up. Since he was an active man as late as in 1442, I find it  less likely that he was born as early as ca. 1350. Hence, I must assume that if the traditio
2 CONC n has a core  of truth, it must be about one of the plagues in the decades after 1350. His ancestry here is based  on the tradition, that is supported by known relations in the following generations.
