1 NOTE {geni:about_me} *
2 CONT Gisele var''' datter af den holstenske adelsmand Hartvig Ottosen Sehested''' (nævnt i kilder mellem 1387–1406) og Mette Segebodsdatter Krummedige. 
2 CONT Hendes '''mor var datter af den mægtige Segebod Krummedige'''.
2 CONT
2 CONT Slægten: Sehested-slægten (oprindeligt Sested) stammer fra Holstein og ejede store godser i både Sønderjylland og på de danske øer.
2 CONT https://clausbechgaard.dk/MineAner/bechgaard/4155.htm
2 CONT
2 CONT Det mest direkte, historiske bevis på hendes eksistens findes i '''rets- og arvedokumenter vedrørende Løgismose''' Gods på Sydvestfyn. https://www.danskeherregaarde.dk/nutid/loegismose
2 CONT
2 CONT Hendes mor, '''Mette Krummedige,''' ejede en stor anpart i Løgismose gods.Da '''moderen døde, overtog Gisele en arvepart i godset sammen med sine brødre, Poppe og Reimer Sehested.'''
2 CONT '''Kildeopsatser bekræfter, at Giseles mand senere opkøbte hendes brødres andele, så parret fik samlet mere af godset under sig.'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT JKM
2 CONT **
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Other owners of L. in the late 1300s were members of the families Krummedige, Sested (Sehestedt) and Jul of Sønderjylland. Erik Krummedige owned a part, and in 1392 his sister fru Elsebe Krummedige's husband Henrik Split gave him 
2 CONC this share besides the share which was hers. Also Erik Krummedige's brother (father?) Segebod Krummedige ( + latest 1397) owned a share, which was inherited by the daughter Mette Segebodsdatter Krummedige, who 1. time was married 
2 CONC to one from the family Jul, the second time to Hartvig Ottosen Sested. Her share was inherited by the sons of 1. marriage Iver (+ earliest 1421), Troels ( + earliest 1401) and Thomas Jul  (+ between 1438-47) and her sons-in-law, m
2 CONC ayor in Flensborg Sivert Krok, mayor in Flensborg Henrik Vrese (Friis) and citizen in Ribe Thetmar von Gatmer, called Blow (Blue). Parts of L. went to her sons of 2. marriage, Poppe and Reimer Hartvigsen Sested and the daughter Gi
2 CONC sele Hartvigsdatter Sested. The last mentioned was married to Jep Wilsen (Ferke) who bought the ownerships from his brothers-in-law Poppe and Reimer.
