2 CONT
2 CONT The book, "Reliques of the Rives (Ryves)" (Lynchburg, VA: J. P. Bell Co., 1929), pp. 1-5, by J. Rives Childs states that Robert Ryves of Blandford, Dorset was born about 1490 and died 11 Feb 1551; purchased Randleston/Ranston in 1
2 CONC 545 and Damory Court at Blandford in 1548; married Joan who died 12 Dec 1560. Their children were:
2 CONT
2 CONT 1 John Ryves (b. 1514; d. 1549) married Amye Harvey of Tarent Launceston 2 Agnes Ryves married John Swayne 3 a daughter married William Hunton
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of John Ryves and Amye Harvey:
2 CONT
2 CONT 1 John Ryves (b. 24 Jun 1536; d. 1587) married Elizabeth Mervyn 2 Mary Ryves (b. c1538) married William Aden alias Barbett 3 Margaret Ryves (b. c1540) married Richard Lawrence 4 Jane Ryves (b. c1542) married Thomas Sydenham 5 Robe
2 CONC rt Ryves (b. c1544; d. 1576) 6 Richard Ryves (b. c1547) 7 Thomas Ryves (b. c1549; d. after 1596)
2 CONT
2 CONT In the eleven children of John Ryves and Elizabeth Mervyn, their third child was Lucy Ryves but she was born about 1561 and married Thomas Bellot.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT https://archive.org/stream/johnhillofdorche00bart#page/n107/mode/1up
2 CONT Pg.96
2 CONT family were born before 1548 . . . . He married first about 1540, Anne, daughter of John Trowbridge of Colyton, Devonshire; she died about 1560; he married second, about 1563, Lucy, daughter of John Ryves of Dorset.
2 CONT Children by first wife:
2 CONT i. Roger,4 b. about 1542, eldest son.
2 CONT ii. ALEXANDER, second son, lived in Taunton; m. Alice, dau. of John Hansard of Lyme Regis, and had issue.
2 CONT iii. ELIZABETH, m. first, a Hobbs; m. second, a Murifey; m. third, a Martin; d. s. p.
2 CONT iv. WILLIAM, d. s. p.
2 CONT v. ROBERT, d. s. p.
2 CONT vi. HENRY, d. s. p.
2 CONT vii. AMBROSE, d. s. p.
2 CONT viii. GABRIEL, living 1592; d. s. p.
2 CONT ix. SUSAN, d. s. p.
2 CONT x. ELEANOR, m. after 1592, a Gravitt.
2 CONT Children by second wife:
2 CONT xi. BENJAMIN, b about 1564; m. and had at least a dau. Anne, living unmarried in 1657, mentioned in the will of her cousin Roger5 Hill of Taunton.
2 CONT xii. LUCY, m. before 1592, William Lawrence of Dorsetshire.
2 CONT xiii. THOMAS, b. about 1568; lived in Chard, where he d. in 1629 probably unmarried. His will, dated Nov. 20, 1628, gives to cousins (i. e. nephews) John Hill and Jonathan Hill, yeomen of Chaffcombe, sons of brother John, 10L each
2 CONC , and 5L more to each on marriage; cousin (i. e. niece) Anne Hill, dau. of brother Benjamin, 5L; to the poor of Pitminster 10s.; residue to friend Thomas Legg of Chard who was executor. [Wells Reg.] [This Thomas Legg of Chard was 
2 CONC also intimate with John and Walter Deane of Chard who came to New England, being a witness and overseer of the will of their father William Deane in 1634.]
2 CONT xiv. John, youngest child, but of age in 1592; b. probably about 1570.
