1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Heir to his grandfather and grandmother was 20 years of age on 24 June 1556 and had a fortune of 20,000 pounds/year, a enormous sum for the time and a considerable part of which was laid out in Dorset. He was the f
2 CONC irst in the family to matriculate at Oxford University where he entered Corpus Christi College in 1547, obtaining a BA in 1551 and was made a fellow in 1554. He received the degree of MA in 1555. He then passed the Middle Temple o
2 CONC f the Inns of Court for the study of law (admitted in January 1555). 
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1560 he purchased the manor of Compton from the Queen (previously belonging to the monastery of Milton for 450 pounds.
