1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Fulforde, William, of Devon, arm. Exeter Coll. matric. 13 Jul 1604, aged 17; bar.-at-law, Middle Temple, 1615 (as 2s. of Thomas, of Fulford, Devon, esq.); baptised at Dunsford 10 Aug., 1600; buried at Bovey Tracey 
2 CONC 10 March, 1638-9; brother of Thomas 1616, and Francis 1599. See Foster's Judges and Barristers.
2 CONT
2 CONT Source: Oxford University Alumni, 1500-1886
2 CONT
2 CONT WILLlAM FULFORD, second son of Thomas F., of Fulford, Devon, esq. Called 8 July 1614 confirmed 3 Feb., 1615-16. Adm. at Middle Temple, 10 Feb. 1606/7.
2 CONT
